to be like a republican senate hearing - let's see if there is someone we
can impeach.

If you think that there was/is some "political tension" between server
designers and chip designers over moving things into the processor chip...
then you are smoking something.  I know the Marvel architect, and the marvel
IO architect, and used to go to the early working design meetings.  Everyone
was excited and enthusiastic about what was being done, and was working
closely with the chip architect.

The truth is that the day that the decision was announced, I heard the
initial version of what Bill calls the "ammended" story.  And within days, I
heard the story directly from the horses mouth.  I did not feel that I could
"replay" this story in public, since it wasn't told to us in a way that
indicated that it should be made public.

Chip builders design chips, system designers design systems.  They both want
to make the best product they can provide.  They both believe strongly in
what they are doing.  Just like people working on VMS believe in our
product.  Could the EV8 design have been the best thing since sliced bread?
Probably.  Just like EV6 was, and just like EV7 will be.  But business isn't
always just about being the best - or Betamax would have won the VCR wars.

The core value of VMS isn't the chip architecture, or being on the absolute
fastest CPU - VMS squanders Alpha chip performance as it is (since we do not
optimize the kernel for each chip generation).





