hello,

answers is : it depends ....

your overall strategy is
1) clone FS -> /clone/FS
 at this time, space of /clone/FS is close to zero,
as time pass /clonse/FS will grow when you modify/write file on /FS
2) do a backup of /clone/FS as quickly as possible
3) delete the clone.

space use by the clone will be up to original space of FS.
but if you modify a small number of file, or the same file many times, space
consumation will not grow that much.

