Hallo MIKA!

 > Hy I have To clone File System To win Time On Backup
 > How Many Space I need To clone My FileSystem.
 > Did i need Exactly the same Space used By the File system
 > On onother Disks to Clone or less .

If you use AdvFS, which I assume, you need only as much file space, as 
much the data on the original file system changes while the clone 
exists, because only that DATA is duplicated that really is different 
on the clone and the master. This means that when you create the clone, 
you need virtually no space at all. But while the clone exists, space 
requirements are growing as data is modified on the master. But if you 
only create the clone right before starting the backup, and delete the 
clone right afterwards, you won't need too much space for it. Depending 
on what you are doing with the master in this time, of course :-).

