> And i still finger users.
> Doeas anoyone Know how to remove the porssiblity Without
> Remove Security Or rename File .

Disabling the finger daemon in /etc/inetd.conf will stop remote sites
from getting output from a command like:

finger @yoursite

It does not prevent local users from issuing the finger command.
However, having updated your /etc/inetd.conf file, you must tell the
inetd daemon to reread the file.  Do this by sending the HUP signal to
inetd process, like this:

ps -ef | grep inetd
kill -HUP <pid>

where <pid> is the process number of the inetd process.

