Dave, since you're concerned primarily with device performance rather
than filesystem performance, I'd use "dd" to the character devices
rather than "cp" to mounted filesystems.  Injecting filesystem, VFS,
and UBC anomalies and inconsistencies won't help the experiment.

WRT to the variations you're seeing, there are many possibilities:

  - Bus contention
  - Controller contention
  - Actuator contention, if more than 1 RAID device is using
    1 spindle (software RAID)
  - RAID devices are using different (i.e. different-speed)
    partitions
  - RAID devices are using different chunk sizes
  - RAID devices' cache policies are different (hardware
    RAID)
  - RAID devices not arranged identically WRT bus/controller loading
  - Experimentation is being done on a system that's already 
    partially-loaded with an unpredictable workload

There's probably more, but there's a start.

QH


