"Lambinon Philippe" <lph@skynet.be> wrote in message
news:3c1f5dcb$0$10217$ba620e4c@news.skynet.be...
> Hi,
>
> I'm relatively novice in the world Tru64? And of course I have a
relatively
> basic question. What is the best way (and complete procedure) to backup a
> full system (installed with AdvFS and LSM) ? I think that we have to use
> 'vdump' ? But what is the complete syntax ? Or can I find a complete
> procedure somewhere ?

man pages for vdump and vrestore can tell you all the details.

The correct procedure would be (providing you have ADVFS-UTILITIES license
and have installed the product):

0. mkdir -p /clones/root /clones/usr

1. clonefset root_domain root root_cl
2. mount -t advfs -o ro root_domain#root_cl /clones/root
3. vdump -0uNC /clones/root
4. umount /clones/root
5. rmfset -f root_domain root_cl

Repeat those steps for /usr

With AdvFS clones you can happily backup while other continue to work. Clone
is a read-only snapshot of the file system.

Nix.




