"Jack Patteeuw" <jpatteeu@ford.com> wrote in message
news:3C0E3C4E.220864A7@ford.com...
> I have an ESA12000 with a pair of HSZ80's.  Each HSZ80 has a pair of
> host access SCSI (wide, differential) ports, for a total of 4 ports.
> Can these 4 ports be connected to 4 different host ?
>
> Has anyone used an HSZ80 with any type of Solaris system ?
>
> Jack

Hi

At least 2 hosts must be possible. Connect host1 to to port1 and host2 to
port2
4 could also be possible, but that depends on the type of configutation you
have.(e.g. multibus failover, tranparent failover).
A HSG80 (fibre channel variant) can be used with a fibre switch/hub. You can
connect many hosts to this controller this way.
I'm not 100% sure, but i think there must be a sort of SCSI hub/switch to
get the same on a HSZ80.

No i did not run it on Solaris yet. (I have HSZ controllers running on AIX
NT/intel and NT/alpha). But except for the point that you need the Solaris
software kit and a advised SCSI controller this cannot be difficult. Just do
what the manual says.

Paul






