Mike Coleman wrote:

> Gemesi Ferenc <gemesif@westel.hu> writes:
>> Dear gurus,
>> '/sbin/showfdmn usr_domain'
>> command is freezing.
> 
> You could attempt to run it under truss, to see what it's doing when it
> freezes.
> 
> --Mike


If this isn't being caused by a hardware I/O problem (that's where my money 
is) and you do need to report it to your local CSC, the determine:

 1)  does this just happen to one domain, or all domains?
 2)  what state are the processes in?
 3)  do other commands hang, like an ls(1) of the file tree?

Before logging a call with the CSC, or rebooting, you should note the pid's of 
a selection of hanging processes and take a peek at where they are locked up 
in dbx.   There may be a common thread eg:

 # dbx -k /vmunix
 (dbx)  set $pid=12345             (replace 12345 with the pid no:)
 (dbx)  trace

repeat for however many hung I/O processes you can find.  Screen grab the 
traces and make a note of which command went with which trace.   When you log 
you call with the CSC you can give this info (if it's a software problem).

Im my experience though, hung commands like showfdmn usually indicate a disk 
problem.

John



