I agree.  Over the past two decades, every problem I can recall that
had symptoms such as those you're seeing had to do with system "iron"
such as power supplies, fans, connectors, and so on.  Here's just one
example: several years ago we had an 8400 that would occasionally halt
for apparently no reason (not crash, but halt).  Cycle the power and
everything would be fine for a few hours.  The cause turned out to be
one single connector in a Molex mate-n-lock that had backed out of its
normal position such that it was not engaging with its mate but rather
just touching it, providing a high-resistance and flaky connection. 
This connector was on the line that powered the main fan and the
white-nylon connector was visible behind the protective screen
(literally "right in front of our noses").  So the first thing I'd do
in your case would be to check and re-seat every power-related
connector in the system to make sure it's doing its thing.  Not a fun
job, but there's a good chance it'll fix what you're seeing.

Good luck,

QH


